# Two polygons partition a square. Their two shared edges produce opposing
# dependencies for an oblique direction; assigning one polygon per rank makes
# a genuine global cell cycle while each owned graph has a single vertex.
# Coordinates are dimensionless; vertex 3 defines the shared inward notch.
# Hand constructed test geometry under the repository MIT license.
o CBCDistributedCycle
v 0.5 0.5 0
v 0.75 0.5 0
v 0.625 0.6 0
v 0.75 0.75 0
v 0.5 0.75 0
f 2 3 1
f 1 3 2 4 5
